Run the launchd disabled-jobs policy without requiring BOOT_PROGRESS.

UniXNU's zzz-boot-progress.patch wraps sheng_boot_watchdog_policy() in
"#if XNU_BOOT_PROGRESS". This board keeps CONFIG_XNU_BOOT_PROGRESS=n because
the drawing path needs the audited Virtio block build, so the policy never
runs and sheng-disable-jobs has no effect. alioth (same 21H461 profile, real
device to the home screen) has BOOT_PROGRESS=y specifically so the policy can
disable liveactivitiesd/cryptexd/routined and stop the daemon crash storm.

sheng_boot_watchdog_policy() itself only writes disabled.plist through plain
syscalls; it has no dependency on the boot-progress drawing code. Remove the
two guard lines so the policy runs whenever Data mount is enabled. The two
boot_progress_stage calls remain - they are weak stubs when BOOT_PROGRESS is
off.
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
@@ -8638,10 +8638,8 @@
 	if (data_error) panic("offline scratch Data mount failed: %d", data_error);
-#if defined(XNU_BOOT_PROGRESS) && XNU_BOOT_PROGRESS
 	extern int sheng_boot_watchdog_policy(void *, uint64_t);
 	boot_progress_stage("temporary watchdog launch policy enter");
 	int policy_error=sheng_boot_watchdog_policy(p, (uint64_t)scratch_addr);
 	if (policy_error) panic("sheng watchdog launch policy failed: %d", policy_error);
 	boot_progress_stage("temporary watchdog launch policy ready");
-#endif
 #endif
 #if CONFIG_MEMORYSTATUS
